WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.386
Every police meeting leaves a record.

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:04.020
Let's talk about it.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:07.701
This year, inspectors found
suppliers holding police data

00:00:07.963 --> 00:00:09.883
breached again and again.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:13.245
At one force, a key
meeting went unrecorded,

00:00:13.549 --> 00:00:16.638
and an AI search invented
a football match.

00:00:17.038 --> 00:00:19.748
In interviews, the official
recorder keeps the master.

00:00:20.122 --> 00:00:23.442
Steno A.I. writes the transcript
and summary on the force's device.

00:00:23.842 --> 00:00:26.242
In briefings, it transcribes live.

00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:30.251
Today, recordings often
sit in suppliers' clouds,

00:00:30.503 --> 00:00:33.028
copied where your force can't see.

00:00:33.798 --> 00:00:35.001
With Steno A.I.,

00:00:35.765 --> 00:00:37.265
they stay on the device,

00:00:37.535 --> 00:00:39.491
kept as long as you decide.

00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:41.498
Reports come out your way:

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:44.637
interview summary,
decision log, case note.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.996
Public AI tools can refuse or
filter sensitive crime content.

00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:51.829
Here, your template runs on your model.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:56.466
Steno A.I. Notes that
stay inside the force.
